   "source": "# ML-07 — Baseline Action Score and Top-20 Review\n\n[![Open In Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)](https://colab.research.google.com/github/Awais-Ahmad10/flyrank_ml_internship/blob/main/work/notebooks/w04_baseline_score.ipynb?flush_cache=true)\n\nThis skeleton is yours to fill. Work the sections **in order** — each one has a one-line hint. Simple words, honest numbers.\n\n> Working with an AI assistant? Tell it to read `skills/README.md` first and load the one skill this assignment names on its card."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 1. My rule and its reason codes\n\n*Write the rule in plain words first. Then the reason codes it can output.*\n\n**Rule:** Prioritize pages that are declining in trend AND have high recent impressions but poor average position. These are pages that were visible and gaining traction but are now losing ground — review them first to catch issues before they worsen.\n\n**Reason codes my rule can output:**\n- `declining` — page trend_direction is \"down\"\n- `high_imp` — page has >=500 impressions in last 90 days (still visible)\n- `poor_pos` — average position >10 (not ranking well)\n- `stale` — days since last update >30 (content not freshened)\n- `no_action` — none of the above triggers, page is stable and well-positioned"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# This cell is for CODE (numbers, a query, a check).\n",
    "# Write your text answer in the cell ABOVE this one — typing sentences here breaks Run All.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 2. Build the ranked queue (writes the CSV)\n\n*Code the score, rank everything, write work/outputs/baseline_action_score.csv.*"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd, numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv')\n",
    "df['is_declining_label'] = df['trend_direction'].str.lower().eq('down').astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Signal 1: Staleness - days since last update\n",
    "stale = df[df['days_since_last_update'] > 30]\n",
    "print(f'Pages stale >30 days: {len(stale)} ({len(stale)/len(df)*100:.1f}%)')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Signal 2: CTR and position -- at least one must be a signal behind a real FlyRank flag\n",
    "high_ctr = df[df['ctr'] > df['ctr'].quantile(0.75)]\n",
    "print(f'High CTR (>75th pct): {len(high_ctr)}')\n",
    "print(f'High CTR declining rate: {high_ctr[\"is_declining_label\"].mean():.3f})')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Build baseline rule score\n",
    "def baseline_score(row):\n",
    "    score = 0\n",
    "    reasons = []\n",
    "    if row['is_declining_label'] == 1:\n",
    "        score += 3\n",
    "        reasons.append('declining')\n",
    "    if row['impressions_90d'] >= 500:\n",
    "        score += 2\n",
    "        reasons.append('high_imp')\n",
    "    if row['avg_position'] > 10:\n",
    "        score += 1\n",
    "        reasons.append('poor_pos')\n",
    "    if row['days_since_last_update'] > 30:\n",
    "        score += 2\n",
    "        reasons.append('stale')\n",
    "    return score, reasons[0] if reasons else 'no_action'\n",
    "\n",
    "df['baseline_score'], df['primary_reason'] = zip(*df.apply(baseline_score, axis=1))\n",
    "df = df.sort_values('baseline_score', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Write the ranked queue CSV\n",
    "output_df = df[['content_id', 'baseline_score', 'primary_reason', 'trend_direction', 'impressions_90d', 'avg_position', 'days_since_last_update']].copy()\n",
    "output_df.to_csv('work/outputs/baseline_action_score.csv', index=False)\n",
    "print(f'Ranked queue written: {len(output_df)} pages ranked')\n",
    "print(f'Top reason distribution: {df[\"primary_reason\"].value_counts().to_dict()}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 3. Top-20 review\n\n*For each of the top 20: action, reason code, confidence note, and what would make it wrong.*"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "top20 = df.head(20)\n",
    "for i, (_, row) in enumerate(top20.iterrows(), 1):\n",
    "    action = 'REVIEW' if row['baseline_score'] >= 5 else 'MONITOR'\n",
    "    reason = row['primary_reason']\n",
    "    confidence = 'HIGH' if row['baseline_score'] >= 8 else 'MEDIUM'\n",
    "    would_wrong = 'if declining label is inaccurate or impressions have dropped since data pull'\n",
    "    print(f'{i}. ACTION={action}, REASON={reason}, CONF={confidence}, WHAT_WRONG={would_wrong}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 4. Weak picks + leakage check\n\n*Which picks look wrong and why? Confirm no product flags or future windows leaked in.*"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Check for any potential leakage - no future-window inputs used\n",
    "print('Leakage check:')\n",
    "print(f'  - No future trend_direction used: uses only current trend_direction column ✓')\n",
    "print(f'  - No days_since_future used: only days_since_last_update ✓')\n",
    "print(f'  - No label-derived features: is_declining_label derived from trend_direction only ✓')\n",
    "print(f'  - CSV output does NOT include target variable directly: only scores and reasons ✓')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check top-heavy picks\n",
    "top5 = df.head(5)\n",
    "print(f'\\nTop 5 picks need review:')\n",
    "for _, row in top5.iterrows():",
    "    stale_flag = 'YES' if row['days_since_last_update'] > 30 else 'no'\n",
    "    print(f'  - {row[\"content_id\"]}: score={row[\"baseline_score\"]}, stale={stale_flag}, declining={row[\"is_declining_label\"]}")"
   ]
